iv style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://files.privateerpress.com/products/models/ArchangelComparison.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> The Archangel the Big Beasty I want to make for myself, with a size comparison to a Angelius and a person.<br /> Familar 5? N/A?</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T15:42:53-07:00","id":266485,"title":"","content":"Hey, you know what's a much better game than Exalted? Iron Kingdoms. You know what's already been designed for compatibility with HORDES, thus making Legion homebrew much easier? Iron Kingdoms.<br /> <br /> (You should play Iron Kingdoms for this stuff instead.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T15:59:46-07:00","id":266490,"title":"","content":"Ranger_Lord that is a bad idea. That doesn't avenge the destruction of the blessed Isle, or the shattering of the pole of earth. That doesn't wring the life from the Infernal exalted and seal them away in a prison like the Sidereal made for the solar that I can abandon in Elsewhere, and leave there helpless, powerless, frozen for all eternity. <br /> <br /> Besides that Technically Exalted does support it. Familiar background and taking an appropriate creature. Take the Rake. Take the large cat from Exalted core, Add the scorpion tail mutation to it. Done. Mechanically the monsters are easy to generate, so easy it is laughable. The question is, can it be done with wyld shaping? Wyld shaping lets me make people or artifacts, so making monsters should be within the realm of possibility right?<br /> <br /> <br /> So anyone else have a good idea on whether or not I can wyld shape up Familiar like monsters using Solar Wyld Shaping to give my inner rage and hate form and substance, so that it can follow me into battle with it's new form and slaughter my foes at my side?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T16:23:29-07:00","id":266497,"title":"","content":"Funny, I literally just started reading FoW: LoE yesterday.<br /> <br /> I would say that Spawn are closer to Genesis Artifacts than extras given that they have no souls or real free will. (They are even called out as biological machines)<br /> <br /> However: You could throw mutations at mundane animals to get most of them so by my reading you can use WST to make them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 09-26-2014, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T16:30:42-07:00","id":266500,"title":"","content":"Thanks Exthalion, I was taking visual design from the Legion and it's visual elements more than anything. They would count as familiar background right? Or as allies? I ask because you need as many successes to shape it as it costs in dots. SO I also need to know if my dot estimations are right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T16:31:07-07:00","id":266501,"title":"","content":"Making the Legion is not something that is truly, directly Solar in theme. Everblight is not some super-Solar. Everblight (and other IK dragons) would probably be best compared to Primordials. <br /> <br /> The closest non-demon non-Infernal thing for Legion is probably Lunars, truth be told. Pretty much all the Legion heroes look like some amalgamation of beast and man in varying quantities.<br /> <br /> Also a DB is not a literal dragon, nor should you interpret dragons in Exalted as anything so banal as a normally-occurring species. You are not going to take the blood from a DB, throw Solar magic at it, and wind up with Drogon, Rhaegal and Viserion. DB blood is human blood in the end. Most dragons Exalted are simply gods whose puissance has led them to express one of the highest possible forms, that of the dragon - a very prevalent notion in Eastern myth and wuxia. Or they're weird animals that are generally kinda draconic in shape but of normal animal intelligence.<br /> <br /> leo if you really want Legion-themed things running around, I think it'd be trivial to insert them as demons, as some weird horrible natural animals, etc. IMO Wyld-Shaping might be able to do it, but you might be overthinking your vector for getting the result you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T16:32:23-07:00","id":266502,"title":"","content":"Well given you can buy magnitudes of people with each dot, perhaps spending successes on each dot of familiar, and then a dot more per essence? And then go by the mdv subtraction stuff from Wyld Cauldron Technique for people to give it rage and hate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T16:37:00-07:00","id":266503,"title":"","content":"Solar God-Kings can create whatever armies they wish given enough XP. However, you haven't mentioned what houserules or even errata version you use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1628-emeraldstreak","name":"emeraldstreak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1628_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T16:42:48-07:00","id":266506,"title":"","content":"@Zelbinnean: When I mentioned the DB I meant our group is one Sidreal - Battles, one Solar -Dawn (me), One DB - Air. I was going to make him a pair of something like the stingers. Maybe use a bit of his blood so they are a part of him, and match his mind rather than mine, and maybe to give them access to a few DB charms like Elemental Bolt that don't require a large essence score.<br /> <br /> @Unkown DarkLord: I hadn't thought of giving them more than awakened essence (And maybe some simple charms) but maybe. That's why I'm asking these questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T16:51:25-07:00","id":266511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/266444-wyld-shaping-a-legion-of-ever-solar-blight?p=266506#post266506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Unkown DarkLord: I hadn't thought of giving them more than awakened essence (And maybe some simple charms) but maybe. That's why I'm asking these questions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Some of their powers such as the fire breathing and the corrosive ash clouds are probably better represented by making them god-blooded and giving them some very specific spirit charms such as Dragon's Suspire. That probably works better for want then DB charms since that opens dangerous doors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T17:15:35-07:00","id":266520,"title":"","content":"From my standpoint (which FWI, has exactly zero knowledge of your source material) everything that you want to do can be done by adding mutations to pre-existing organisms. Even the acid/fire-spitting. If you haven't done so already, I suggest reading Compass: Wyld. It has a ton of mutations that may help you figure out how to do what you're aiming for. <br /> <br /> For the logistics, I, as an ST, would be fine with a player Wyld-Shaping up groups of mildly mutated beasts, though larger/more heavily mutated ones I would require to be made as biological artifacts, as per the Wonders of the Lost Age guidelines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T17:24:37-07:00","id":266522,"title":"","content":"In this case Noodle, almost 0 knowelge of source material is needed. Stingers are about man sized, A raek is about tiger sized, an Angelius is about Larger beast (think River Dragon or Claw Strider) sized, and I'd guess the Arch Angel is about Behemoth sized, so stats like a really big Tyrant Lizard, with wings and fire breath.<br /> <br /> Which would mean learning Craft: Genisis. Damn I was trying to avoid that. My dawn caste doesn't have craft as a favored skill.<br /> <br /> Oh and to answer the question we are using 2.5e which is why everything is all post RotSE, and the creation looks like hell at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 09-26-2014, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T17:47:45-07:00","id":266531,"title":"","content":"Revild\u2019s mutation and genesis revision (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zSae7JJfkkLrgrDu5sNPzNrYBQFAO7EjSaMs4OPvDXo/edit\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...Ms4OPvDXo/edit</a>) will work but you would need to give up on Wyld Shaping for this. It does have everything you need and with the new Solar charm (tier three) he added it shouldn't be too hard.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2580-quasit17","name":"quasit17","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T17:53:34-07:00","id":266532,"title":"","content":"If it were another game I might say yes. But something like this, I know the ST wouldn't approve of Quasit, thanks though. I'll keep it in mind. Basicly we aren't allowed to use any house rules. The Wyldshaping up monsters to control would be bending the rules but not creating new ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T19:06:23-07:00","id":266559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/266444-wyld-shaping-a-legion-of-ever-solar-blight?p=266522#post266522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this case Noodle, almost 0 knowelge of source material is needed. Stingers are about man sized, A raek is about tiger sized, an Angelius is about Larger beast (think River Dragon or Claw Strider) sized, and I'd guess the Arch Angel is about Behemoth sized, so stats like a really big Tyrant Lizard, with wings and fire breath.<br /> <br /> Which would mean learning Craft: Genisis. Damn I was trying to avoid that. My dawn caste doesn't have craft as a favored skill.<br /> <br /> Oh and to answer the question we are using 2.5e which is why everything is all post RotSE, and the creation looks like hell at the moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. Poor word choice on my part. I meant for you to Wyld shape up the bigger ones just like the small ones. Only, instead of shaping them as people/beasts, you shape them as artifacts. And what artifact level they are should probably be determined by the guidelines for biological artifacts in Wonders of the Lost Age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T20:08:27-07:00","id":266575,"title":"","content":"Oh! thank you Noodle that does help, but also wasn't quite clear. When I look at the artifact option for shaping it says I need the relevant craft skill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T22:02:53-07:00","id":266639,"title":"","content":"As for Everblight himself, IK dragons seem like Behemoths to me, whose true forms are, well, rocks. Everblight, given his cunning and scientific mindset, is probably the custom Charm genius among his siblings, focusing on deliberate control of his Blight abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T06:16:29-07:00","id":266730,"title":"","content":"So your saying my Solar who will be taking on this role and becoming the father of his legion and granting command over the monstrosities forged by his hand to 2 of his fellow inmates that escaped with him, should be developing custom charms?<br /> <br /> remember I'm not the ST, I'm a player, if I was the ST I could hand wave this and be done. These monsters are for me as a player, so that our very damaged creation can stand a chance it is why I will be trying to forge my Arch Angel, something big and mean enough, and powerful enough to be classified as a Solar Behemoth. We are talking a creation where sadly star metal is now as easy to come by as jade because of the slaughter that happened in Yu Shan. That is the setting I'm playing in. A setting where there are so few exalted left, Creation has only 2 sidereals, and all exalted answer directly to the new Sun, Sol Vindictive. I'm going to guess there are maybe 20 active Solars any more, and a hand full of Lunar. Forget 10,000 dragon blooded, we more like 100.<br /> <br /> We don't know what is keeping the Fair Folk from running rough shod all over creation, but, right now that's my big worry since I found out my teams mission in our back-story did succeed (we managed to recapture the P. Womb from Malfeas), and apparently the agents of the Abyss are too busy with internal struggles to attack creation for the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T07:09:58-07:00","id":266739,"title":"","content":"Oh, I did not realize you weren't the ST.<br /> <br /> And in all likelihood...yes. A couple to communicate with the commanders mentally and a couple for the Blight effect, though yours is probably going to involve different themes from Everblight himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T07:22:52-07:00","id":266743,"title":"","content":"Yep. I just like the shape of his monsters.<br /> <br /> Though I am thinking rather than Acidic blight fire, burning golden sun fire. Our Siddie is wondering if I can make the claws or teeth, or stingers out of iron to make sure they can ravage fair folk better. I don't think so and not risk the too wyld for creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 09-27-2014, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T10:03:59-07:00","id":266824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/266444-wyld-shaping-a-legion-of-ever-solar-blight?p=266730#post266730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So your saying my Solar who will be taking on this role and becoming the father of his legion and granting command over the monstrosities forged by his hand to 2 of his fellow inmates that escaped with him, should be developing custom charms?<br /> <br /> remember I'm not the ST, I'm a player, if I was the ST I could hand wave this and be done. These monsters are for me as a player, so that our very damaged creation can stand a chance it is why I will be trying to forge my Arch Angel, something big and mean enough, and powerful enough to be classified as a Solar Behemoth. We are talking a creation where sadly star metal is now as easy to come by as jade because of the slaughter that happened in Yu Shan. That is the setting I'm playing in. A setting where there are so few exalted left, Creation has only 2 sidereals, and all exalted answer directly to the new Sun, Sol Vindictive. I'm going to guess there are maybe 20 active Solars any more, and a hand full of Lunar. Forget 10,000 dragon blooded, we more like 100.<br /> <br /> We don't know what is keeping the Fair Folk from running rough shod all over creation, but, right now that's my big worry since I found out my teams mission in our back-story did succeed (we managed to recapture the P. Womb from Malfeas), and apparently the agents of the Abyss are too busy with internal struggles to attack creation for the moment.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If everyone remaining is Elder that's not so bad.<br /> <br /> Without homebrew, Solars wyld shape armies with mutations, add additional mutations (presumably more situational) with Solar Circle Sorcery (ie Fountain of Fathomless Dreams). Eclipses (and optionally all castes) can wield Grace Magic to turn mortals into 1-dot behemoths and add even more mutations/mutation keyword fey powers, but that's somewhat XP intensive and it's better to simply enslave your own Fey to do it for you.<br /> <br /> Relying on mutations has some major benefits over relying on charms in games featuring serious combat as they cannot be shut down by Solar Circle Sorcery or the Greater Sign of Venus. For instance, if you protect an area with Abjuration of the Maidens and have high-statted behemoth servants guard it, attacking it won't be a cakewalk. This is not to say you cannot bestow your creations charms, it can be done in numerous ways.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?681406-Exalted-2e-Mutation-abuse&amp;s=f21125046f9935cf504e10f2038eaaee&amp;p=16594928#post16594928\" target=\"_blank\">A bit more on mutations</a>. Mind you, Merits can also boost mortal servants significantly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1628-emeraldstreak","user":"emeraldstreak","date":". 09-27-2014, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1628-emeraldstreak","name":"emeraldstreak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1628_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T12:27:33-07:00","id":266947,"title":"","content":"basically, your dawn doesn't have to be the crafter, he just has to control the one doing the crafting and mind raping a raksha noble would be a great place to start, hell, mind rape a few of them and turn them into living pieces of armor that are specialized for a specific task outside of actual combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T12:56:18-07:00","id":266959,"title":"","content":"Yeah I was looking at that. the Charm Dragon's Surprise is no where near as good as the mutation Dragon's Breath.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}